# Lab 04 — TIG Stack + Model-Driven Telemetry (MDT)

**Blueprint mapping:** 4.5 Model-Driven Telemetry (Domain 4.0 Operations)

End-to-end MDT pipeline: Cisco IOS-XE (c8000v on containerlab) streams CPU utilization via **dial-out gRPC/kvGPB** to a **T**elegraf → **I**nfluxDB → **G**rafana stack running in Docker Compose. The subscription is configured programmatically via **NETCONF** (ncclient, `Cisco-IOS-XE-mdt-cfg` model), not CLI.

```
c8000v (172.30.30.11, VRF clab-mgmt)
   │  dial-out gRPC :57000, kvGPB, yang-push, 5s
   ▼
Telegraf (inputs.cisco_telemetry_mdt) ──► InfluxDB 2.x (bucket: mdt) ──► Grafana (Flux)
```

## Components

| Component | Where | Port |
|---|---|---|
| c8000v 17.15.04c (vrnetlab) | containerlab `clab-enauto-iosxe-01` | mgmt 172.30.30.11 |
| Telegraf 1.34 | compose `telegraf` | 57000/tcp (gRPC receiver) |
| InfluxDB 2.7 | compose `influxdb` | 8086 (org `lab`, bucket `mdt`) |
| Grafana 11.2 | compose `grafana_enauto` | **3001** → 3000 |

## Files

- `docker-compose.yml` — the three-service stack
- `telegraf/telegraf.conf` — `inputs.cisco_telemetry_mdt` (grpc, `:57000`) → `outputs.influxdb_v2`
- `mdt_config.py` — ncclient script: reads existing subscriptions (`get_config`), pushes subscription 1 (`edit_config`)

## Bring-up

```bash
# 1. Router (from repo root)
sudo containerlab deploy -t containerlab/enauto.clab.yml --reconfigure

# 2. Stack
cd labs/04-operations/TIG
docker compose up -d
```

Enable NETCONF on the router (one-time per deploy; takes ~1–2 min to initialize, first connect on 830 may be refused — retry):

```
conf t
 netconf-yang
end
copy run start
```

## Configure the subscription (NETCONF)

```bash
python mdt_config.py
```

Pushes to `Cisco-IOS-XE-mdt-cfg`:

| Leaf | Value |
|---|---|
| subscription-id | 1 |
| stream | yang-push |
| encoding | encode-kvgpb |
| period | 500 centiseconds (5 s) |
| xpath | `/process-cpu-ios-xe-oper:cpu-usage/cpu-utilization/five-seconds` |
| source-vrf | `clab-mgmt` |
| receiver | `grpc-tcp://172.30.30.1:57000` |

Equivalent CLI (for reference — the exam tests both forms):

```
telemetry ietf subscription 1
 encoding encode-kvgpb
 filter xpath /process-cpu-ios-xe-oper:cpu-usage/cpu-utilization/five-seconds
 stream yang-push
 update-policy periodic 500
 source-vrf clab-mgmt
 receiver ip address 172.30.30.1 57000 protocol grpc-tcp
```

## Verify

```
! router
show telemetry ietf subscription 1            ! State: Valid
show telemetry ietf subscription 1 receiver   ! State: Connected
```

```bash
# host
docker logs telegraf --tail 20    # no gRPC errors = flowing
```

InfluxDB Data Explorer (`http://localhost:8086`, bucket `mdt`): measurement `Cisco-IOS-XE-process-cpu-oper:cpu-usage/cpu-utilization`, field `five_seconds`, tags `source`, `subscription`, `path`. New point every 5 s.

Grafana (`http://localhost:3001`): InfluxDB datasource — query language **Flux**, URL `http://influxdb:8086`, org `lab`, token from compose, bucket `mdt`.

```flux
from(bucket: "mdt")
  |> range(start: -10m)
  |> filter(fn: (r) => r.subscription == "1")
  |> filter(fn: (r) => r._field == "five_seconds")
```

## Gotchas hit live (the actual lessons)

1. **vrnetlab c8000v puts Gi1 in VRF `clab-mgmt`** behind QEMU user-mode NAT. The global RIB is empty; the VRF holds `10.0.0.0/24` + default via `10.0.0.2`. Any traffic the router originates (including MDT dial-out) must be VRF-aware.
2. **Outbound ICMP dies in the NAT; TCP passes.** `ping 172.30.30.1` fails forever — test reachability with `telnet 172.30.30.1 57000 /vrf clab-mgmt` instead.
3. **`source-vrf` is mandatory** in the subscription (CLI keyword / `<source-vrf>` leaf under `<base>` in the YANG model). Without it the receiver never connects: `% Destination unreachable`.
4. **Receiver IP = the clab management bridge IP on the host** (`172.30.30.1`) — Docker's published port 57000 answers on the bridge address, so the router reaches Telegraf without joining the compose network.
5. **ncclient raw-string payloads:** the `<config>` wrapper must carry `xmlns="urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:netconf:base:1.0"` or the device rejects with `unknown-element: config`.
6. **`containerlab --reconfigure` wipes device config.** `copy run start` protects against reloads only; after a redeploy, re-run `mdt_config.py` — the script is the source of truth.